mill-liberty-3.logic.r1: argue/readings: what the text leaves unstated is read 3 ways: mill-liberty-3.logic.r1 has "is_orig" and "¬could_see → ¬feel_use" and "indifferent ∧ ¬feel_use → natural" and "first ∧ good_from_orig → O more_left"; mill-liberty-3.logic.r1.2 has "is_orig" and "¬could_see → ¬feel_use" and "indifferent ∧ ¬feel_use → natural" and "first ∧ good_from_orig → more_left"; they differ when only "unoriginal minds could see what originality would do for them", "what would do this for them is originality", "unoriginal minds can feel the use of originality", "nearly all, at heart, think they can do very well without originality, though no one says it is not to be admired", "this indifference is too natural to be wondered at", "nothing was ever yet done which some one was not the first to do", "all good things which exist are the fruits of originality" and "it ought to be that there is something still left for originality to accomplish" are true, which the first allows; mill-liberty-3.logic.r1.3 has "is_orig"
